[1] SO(3) → SO(2) splitting (squash background ε ≠ 0)

  The squash axis = 2-axis preserves SO(2) = U(1).

  The 5 components of spin-2 are classified by SO(2) charge m:
    m=0  : T₁ = diag(1,1,-2)/√6  [1 mode]   (squash singlet)
    m=±2 : T₂,T₃                  [2 modes]  (0-1 plane doublet)
    m=±1 : T₄,T₅                  [2 modes]  (off-squash-axis doublet)

  ε=0: all 5 components degenerate (Schur, known result (App D.9))
  ε≠0: splits into at most 3 distinct masses
    H₁₁^q(ε), H₂₂^q(ε) = H₃₃^q(ε), H₄₄^q(ε) = H₅₅^q(ε)

  SO(2) transformation test (θ=π/6):
